=== TITLE: USG Hepatobiliary System (HBS) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL HEPATOBILIARY SYSTEM ULTRASOUND STUDY.
- Normal liver size, gall bladder, and biliary channels without calculus or mass.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: ULTRASONOGRAPHY OF HEPATOBILIARY SYSTEM (HBS)

FINDINGS:
- LIVER: Normal in size and shape. Parenchymal echotexture is uniform and homogeneous. No focal hepatic lesion or intrahepatic biliary radicle dilatation (IHBRD) seen.
- GALL BLADDER: Well-distended with clear acoustic lumen. Wall thickness is normal (2.2 mm). No cholelithiasis, polyp, or sludge.
- COMMON BILE DUCT (CBD): Normal in caliber, measuring 3.4 mm.
- PORTAL VEIN: Normal caliber (10.2 mm) with normal hepatopetal flow on Color Doppler.
- PANCREAS: Visualized head, body, and tail demonstrate normal size and echotexture.